        <section id="intro">
            <h2>Introduction to GTA San Andreas 2026 Edition<span class="citation">[web:1]</span></h2>
            <p>Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas remains one of the most iconic games in gaming history. Released originally in 2004, it has seen numerous updates, with the Definitive Edition bringing modern enhancements. In 2026, the latest version for Android, around v2.11.311, includes bug fixes, improved graphics, and better mobile optimization.<span class="citation">[web:5][web:7]</span></p>
            <p>The game follows CJ''s journey through a vast state inspired by California and Nevada, featuring three major cities: Los Santos, San Fierro, and Las Venturas. Recent patches like 1.112 on PC and 1.87 on mobile have addressed longstanding issues.<span class="citation">[web:2]</span></p>
            <p>This blog covers everything from story to installation, ensuring you''re ready for the latest experience.<span class="citation">[web:11]</span></p>
        </section>

        <section id="history">
            <h2>Game History and Evolution<span class="citation">[web:11]</span></h2>
            <p>GTA San Andreas launched on PlayStation 2 in 2004, selling over 27 million copies. It expanded the series with RPG elements like customizable characters and skills. The mobile port arrived in 2013, followed by the Definitive Edition in 2021 with upgraded visuals.<span class="citation">[web:11]</span></p>
            <p>By 2026, updates continue: Android got v1.87 in November 2025, fixing traffic and FPS issues. PC version 1.112 added classic lighting toggles.<span class="citation">[web:2][web:3]</span></p>
            <p>Rockstar''s ongoing support keeps it relevant, with modding communities thriving.<span class="citation">[web:15]</span></p>
        </section>

        <section id="story">
            <h2>Main Storyline Overview<span class="citation">[web:11]</span></h2>
            <p>Carl "CJ" Johnson returns to Los Santos after his mother''s death. He reunites with brother Sweet and friends Big Smoke and Ryder in Grove Street Families gang.<span class="citation">[web:11]</span></p>
            <p>Betrayals lead CJ to San Fierro, where he runs a garage, fights the Loco Syndicate, and works for agent Mike Toreno. In Las Venturas, casinos and mafia conflicts arise.<span class="citation">[web:11]</span></p>
            <p>Back in Los Santos, CJ confronts traitors, culminating in a chase with corrupt officer Tenpenny. The narrative explores gang life, loyalty, and power.<span class="citation">[web:11][web:16]</span></p>
        </section>
