<p>Always make sure you’re using the latest version of the PPSSPP emulator. New updates come with bug fixes, improved graphics rendering, and speed optimizations. Visit the official PPSSPP website or Play Store to update your app.</p><h2>2. Change Graphics Settings</h2>

<p>Go to <b>Settings → Graphics</b> and apply the following changes:</p>

<ul>

  <li>Mode: <b>Buffered Rendering</b></li>

  <li>Frame Skipping: <b>1 or 2</b></li>

  <li>Auto Frameskip: <b>Enabled</b></li>

  <li>Prevent FPS from exceeding 60: <b>Enabled</b></li>

  <li>Rendering Resolution: <b>1x PSP</b></li>

  <li>Hardware Transform: <b>Enabled</b></li>

</ul>

<p>These adjustments reduce graphical load and make gameplay smoother, especially on mid-range phones.</p><h2>3. Disable Unnecessary Features</h2>

<p>Turn off post-processing shaders, mipmapping, and scaling filters unless necessary. These features may make the graphics look better but significantly reduce performance.</p><h2>4. Adjust System Settings</h2>

<ul>

  <li>Fast Memory (unstable): <b>ON</b></li>

  <li>Multithreaded (experimental): <b>ON</b></li>

  <li>I/O on thread: <b>ON</b></li>

  <li>Change CPU Clock: <b>200 MHz</b></li>

</ul>

<p>These tweaks optimize performance and load game data faster.</p><h2>5. Use Compressed Games (ISO/CSO)</h2>

<p>Using smaller file sizes reduces the load time and memory usage. You can compress your PSP game ISOs into CSO format using ZArchiver or similar tools.</p><h2>6. Clear Cache and Background Apps</h2>

<p>Close other running apps and clear cache before starting PPSSPP. This frees up RAM and improves performance during gameplay.</p><h2>7. Use External Storage</h2>

<p>Install your PPSSPP emulator and store games on an SD card with high read speed. This reduces lag caused by internal memory limitations.</p><h2>8. Download PPSSPP Gold</h2>

<p>PPSSPP Gold offers better performance, fewer ads, and supports the developers. You can download it below after a short countdown.</p><div id="countdown-box">

  <p>Preparing your download... Please wait <span id="countdown">15</span> seconds.</p>

